{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0","id":422542,"title":"Speculation: Changeling Courts 2.0","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-27T20:31:35-08:00","id":422542,"title":"Speculation: Changeling Courts 2.0","content":"As said in title, I thought some speculation on Changeling Courts in 2.0 is going to work might be fun.<br /> <br /> So what courts are going to be included in the book do you think? I mean we know a 1001 nights theme is going to be in it, and I think Miami will keep the Seasonal Courts, but what about Budapest, what about Tokyo, and Cape Town (that's in South Africa right?).<br /> <br /> My guess is TO gets 1001 Nights, Miami gets Seasonal, Budapest gets Moon/Sun, Cape Town gets an exotic African Court System, Tokyo gets the directional courts.<br /> <br /> How about Mantle Merit and any other court merits like court goodwill? As I understand it there will be just 1 Court Mantle Merit, but it will be more free form like Mystery Cult merit.<br /> <br /> Court Contracts, what do you guys think those will be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:42:59-08:00","id":423503,"title":"","content":"Well, the thing about the old courts was that, while Directional Courts were technically <i>there</i>, the skewing of contracts was laughable. Each seasonal court got 3 different sets of contracts, while all the Directional Courts had to share the same contract. Did I mention that Spring gets the ONLY decent healing spell with no massive drawback? The court contracts, in general, were just more powerful than everyone else's contracts. (Which is probably specifically because they were so exclusive - they were the reward for putting up with a court.)<br /> <br /> I think that not having contract &quot;lines&quot; will help things. Rather than a massive block of contracts, you might have a giant grab-bag of contracts, and they might be divvied out between the different courts of any given court system, with maybe a few left-outs, and a few special snowflakes only fitting for a specific type of court. (I.E. that fire laser thing in Eternal Summer might be for Summer and Sun but not for anything Directional.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:32:09-08:00","id":423664,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but reading the outline it's says 1 or 2 unique court contracts so I think court contracts will still be in. I know a contract will not be made up of 5 clauses that have to taken in order of lowest dot to highest dot anymore, but old contracts clauses, the good ones, might be made into thier own contracts. <br /> <br /> So take Dreaming Contract from 1e, maybe the 1 dot clause for navigating the hedge becomes it's own contract,and the 4 dot clause becomes it's own contract. <br /> <br /> I looked at the outline and authors get roughly 5000 words each and 10 or 11 of the old contracts each, which at 250 words each roughly means they it's likely more then 1 clause per 1e contract will be converted into a 2e contract, just based on the math.<br /> <br /> That's not mentioning that some clauses might become seeming bonuses. So far vainglory for example maybe the clause that causes fear becomes the Darkling bonus to Vainglory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T19:15:25-08:00","id":423687,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, &quot;<b>unique</b> court contracts&quot; might be the key, here. That is, you have a big pool of court contracts that most court systems will divvy up between their respective courts, and then a handful of unique court contracts that are specific to that particular court. <br /> <br /> That is, you might have an anger/war related contract, and have it common to Summer and West (of the Directional) since they have similar domain over those sorts of concepts, and in a Dusk/Dawn court, it might go to Dusk if it is especially destructive, or maybe Dawn if it is related to inspiration. <br /> <br /> Hence, no matter what court system you choose, you don't have to make up a giant list of contracts to go with them, and players aren't getting barred access to a huge block of cool powers. You just all get together when making up a court, and divvy up the common court contracts by the themes of the court, then maybe add a couple uniques to add flavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T22:42:02-08:00","id":423858,"title":"","content":"So far as Mantle goes, they all pretty much followed the same general path (excluding the useless Autumn mantle). <br /> <br /> 1 dot: You get +1 to the most relevant application of a skill to the court.<br /> 3 dot: Another +1 to something more broad and useful, or a coupon for skills or merits<br /> 5 dot: Reroll the 1 dot skill, or +1 to something useful almost all the time.<br /> <br /> I suspect there will be a &quot;build a mantle&quot; ruleset that generally follows something similar in scope. Generally, it's a merit you have to buy in tiers, and has other benefits, so it won't give benefits more mechanically powerful than the EXP it takes to buy the mantle in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:48:25-08:00","id":424192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0?p=423858#post423858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect there will be a &quot;build a mantle&quot; ruleset that generally follows something similar in scope. Generally, it's a merit you have to buy in tiers, and has other benefits, so it won't give benefits more mechanically powerful than the EXP it takes to buy the mantle in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I suspect it will look a lot like the &quot;Mystery Cult Initiation&quot; merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:57:18-08:00","id":424267,"title":"","content":"So Mantle will likely be:<br /> <br /> 1 dot- Skill Speciality related to the courts interests<br /> 2 Dot- a 1 dot merit related to court theme<br /> 3 dot- a 2 dot merit related to court theme<br /> 4 dot- a three dot merit related to theme<br /> 5 dot- another three dot merit, or something special that expands on the courts theme.<br /> <br /> Of course unlike Mystery Cult Initiation it will likely boost social rolls with court members and the dots in mantle will likely be added to court contract rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:43:41-08:00","id":424374,"title":"","content":"I suspect it needn't be an outright merit - We're talking outright magic, here, so they may be weak powers somewhat like a kith's power. Keep in mind, Summer's mantle involved outright +1 armor and +1 health. Winters applied a malus to other people's perception rolls by contrast. The Hunter Status merit also gave mostly a ton of merit bonuses (mostly social), even in 1e, while Changeling Mantle mostly directly affected the character, as it was the difference between <i>knowing a guy</i>, and an innate aspect of your own power. <br /> <br /> Also, there were a lot of skill bonuses, rather than merits for much the same reason. In terms of EXP, specialties are equal to a 1 dot merit, and skill dots are 2-dot merits. Pledges, interestingly, worked in much the same way - each +1 of a pledge was just 2 EXP in benefit.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, there was the special mantle bonus for the crowns of the monarchs, like Summers adding Mantle dots to Initiative, or Autumns having Harvest of Whispers add bonus glamour for contracts. Obviously, not everyone gets one of those, but they'd need mechanical guidelines, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:57:52-08:00","id":424407,"title":"","content":"each possible mantle won't be written up, so its likely to be relative generic, I looked up the Mystery Initiation Merit and took the basic shape from that then added the most universal elements of the previous mantle merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:13:49-08:00","id":424417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0?p=424407#post424407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">each possible mantle won't be written up, so its likely to be relative generic, I looked up the Mystery Initiation Merit and took the basic shape from that then added the most universal elements of the previous mantle merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each possible mantle, no, but if you think that they'll ignore giving a sample, and making it for the most popular courts people are likely to want to see, (seasonal, definitely, and likely at least directional, as well,) you're kidding yourself.<br /> <br /> The point of the Mystery Cult is that it's something that could be found in a million varieties, and would generally be a &quot;monster of the week&quot; antagonist. Courts are major and established and something you deal with diplomatically. They could easily have a &quot;make your own hunter status benefits&quot;, too, but each hunter compact and conspiracy has its own detailed status benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:08:46-08:00","id":424722,"title":"","content":"I guess its possible that have a generic court mantle merit, so you could build your own, and then detail what each dot grants you in each of the cities court system in the respective cities section. just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:25:14-08:00","id":424731,"title":"","content":"FWIW, Mantle will be a Merit. It'll look a little like Mystery Cult Initiation, but definitely its own thing. <br /> <br /> Tokyo won't have Directional Courts. I have a different thing in mind for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:03:03-08:00","id":425745,"title":"","content":"Godzilla courts, with a Godzilla Court, Mothra Court ect ... :-) I kid of course. I'm really looking forward to this book, I'm dying of curiousity .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:32:14-08:00","id":425942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0?p=425745#post425745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Godzilla courts, with a Godzilla Court, Mothra Court ect ... :-) I kid of course. I'm really looking forward to this book, I'm dying of curiousity .</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas no. My kaiju film references are mostly sequestered to Forsaken 2e. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:06:52-08:00","id":426041,"title":"","content":"If you add new Courts, <i>please</i> take pains to tie them into the central abuse metaphor of the game as a whole. The Seasonal Courts as a whole work as well as they do because they're so in-theme; try to make everything else live up to that standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:40:55-08:00","id":430201,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more variation in court systems. We have (That I can recall), Seasonal, Directional, and Day/Night, which are all neatly quartered and symmetrical. How about some 3 or 5 way court systems? In my home game, I am trying out a 3 way system based on time (Past, Present, Future). Maybe we could have a court system based on Body/Mind/Spirit, or based on the Classical Chinese elements (Wood/Fire/Earth/Metal/Water) or even the 7 Chakrahs. <br /> <br /> Or, relating to what atamajakki says, Courts based on the stages of grief/recovery. Come to think of it, that one would be really interesting, as they are already heavily tied with specific emotions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:16:54-08:00","id":430236,"title":"","content":"@andreamus: Freeholds with seven Courts seems to be the easiest to deal with. Just give them rule over a day of the week each and you're golden!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:16:22-08:00","id":430391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0?p=426041#post426041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you add new Courts, <i>please</i> take pains to tie them into the central abuse metaphor of the game as a whole. The Seasonal Courts as a whole work as well as they do because they're so in-theme; try to make everything else live up to that standard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Survival metaphor - they're intentionally going broader than &quot;abuse&quot; in 2E - many of the True Fae can thought of more as traumatic or transformative &quot;events&quot; than victimizers, though that is still there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:28:04-08:00","id":430868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0?p=430391#post430391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Survival metaphor - they're intentionally going broader than &amp;quot;abuse&amp;quot; in 2E - many of the True Fae can thought of more as traumatic or transformative &amp;quot;events&amp;quot; than victimizers, though that is still there too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I don't think I like that; one of Changeling's strengths was the strength of that core metaphor (much like Wraith and depression), and I'd hate to see that go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:52:47-08:00","id":430899,"title":"","content":"I'm sure one.could.still interrupt the game through that lens if one choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T18:02:50-08:00","id":430947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0?p=426041#post426041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you add new Courts, <i>please</i> take pains to tie them into the central abuse metaphor of the game as a whole. The Seasonal Courts as a whole work as well as they do because they're so in-theme; try to make everything else live up to that standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a particularly sane move, it's now a survival metaphor rather than just an abuse metaphor. Victims of Katrina, children of seperate parents, fans of that one Tomb Raider reboot, and quite a few more people of various backgrounds can find commonality in the game without getting hit so hard in the face with a painful subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:07:01-07:00","id":434067,"title":"","content":"Link to where it says that? I'm curious, and also hoping they don't WoDify it too much for 2e. I like a lot of the C:TL themes and mechanics much more than I do some of the other splats like Vampires and Werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5282-the-laurent","name":"The Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:25:24-07:00","id":434152,"title":"","content":"...WoDify it?<br /> <br /> Yer gonna have to explain that, because it makes little sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T10:40:44-07:00","id":434195,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about what WODify means as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:08:20-07:00","id":434216,"title":"","content":"I actually just got done reading through some of the Brainspew discussions for 2.0 and feel a bit better. I think there are a few wonky things there, and I'm sure that the grab-bag nature of the contracts might lead to optimizers and people who like gaming the system having characters with a bunch of random, unrelated powers, but you can't design around the fact that some people are going to abuse any system.<br /> <br /> Now, as for what I meant by 'WODify' well, in some ways I'm talking about in terms of themes, but some things I see in other World of Darkness books that don't really interest me. End Times/End of the World stuff, for one. Equinox Road was really interesting and I think that part of that, and Changeling as a whole, is the more personal nature of the journey, rather than this epic cosmological battle involving, say, Exarchs, or the apocalypse, or so on. As well, I liked the Court system as the chaotic, variable, non-unified thing it was, and I'm hoping that sticks. I look at Mage or Vampires and it's like, 'A small handful of orders, worldwide?' The grand narrative between a small number of castes and a foe, for instance, always left me a bit cold. Whereas, even just counting the Courts we're given, there are the four seasons (which got the most love but a ST can totally help other Courts out), 4 directions, day and night, and then another on a similar *sort* of theme but very different, and then there are suggestions to make your own, hints at some other ideas (I think they mention political parties offhand) and plenty of variety to create this chaotic, really vibrant world, whereas there's always that temptation to pare things down: Five clans (with sub-bloodlines) and seven Covenants, or five orders versus two evil (or at least antagonistic) orders (Seers and Banishers) and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> It's that element, as well as the interesting side-powers (I could play some really interesting Changelings without taking a dot in any contract using things like Pledges, Talecrafting, hedgspun items and token-mongering).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, seeing as they mentioned that they're going to be cutting down the number of custom Court Contracts to one for the core book in order to fit more Courts...I might be worrying over nothing.<br /> <br /> WoDify probably was a bad phrase for it, but I was introduced to the World of Darkness via old Vampires and several things like it, and it never really clicked with me until I read Changeling: The Lost. So I'm mostly talking about those elements of world of darkness that I had seen (even if they aren't, actually) as 'typical.' Which is probably a bad way to phrase it, so apologies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5282,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5282-the-laurent","user":"The Laurent","date":".  Clarification. 03-09-2015, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5282-the-laurent","name":"The Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:18:47-07:00","id":434456,"title":"","content":"I now understand, and yet I am still bewildered.<br /> <br /> For now, I'll just say no need to worry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:11:03-07:00","id":439382,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed playing characters who might be seriously disturbed, but with a good reason. Then figuring out through play whether they figured out how to deal with everything or not. I hope the game retains a good deal of that at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5315-serenity","name":"Serenity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T09:35:58-07:00","id":440015,"title":"","content":"About Mantles.<br /> <br /> I remember reading somewhere, on this forum even, that courts might now have two or three mantles and those would be tied into the court contracts somehow?(like autumn would have a &quot;chilly, dying leaves, and harvest&quot; related mantle and a &quot;scare the fuck out of ya mantle&quot; and they'd be tied to the fleeting and eternal autumn contracts)<br /> <br /> Does anyone else remember reading anything like that, or am I remembering things that didn't happen again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:16:51-07:00","id":440102,"title":"","content":"I don't remember seeing that, but it wouldn't be implausible. It's a way that could jive with some bits from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">the outline</a>. Though the outline's a little nebulous on what exactly they're doing with Court Contracts and Mantles, it seems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2e C:tL Outline</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mantle should be a Merit. It needs to be generic enough to use with anything, with room for a little customization. We can\u2019t reproduce it individually for every court in the book, so we\u2019ve got to be stingy with words.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Court Contracts (Eloy):<br /> These are specific to courts, so every city has one or two unique ones. You should have a real simple guideline system here. But these are NOT going here; they go with the sample courts in the courts chapter.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Court Building should be meaty. Remember, build the roles, and work around that. You need a simple way to handle Mantle, which is essentially your adherence to the Tale. It should be adaptive, like Mystery Cult Initiation, since it\u2019s different in every city.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Missed mention of Mantle as a Merit 03-13-2015, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:24:43-07:00","id":440111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serenity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422542-speculation-changeling-courts-2-0?p=439382#post439382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoyed playing characters who might be seriously disturbed, but with a good reason. Then figuring out through play whether they figured out how to deal with everything or not. I hope the game retains a good deal of that at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Survivors tend to be disturbed individuals, no worries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>