Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ttp://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aladdin<br /> <br /> I did not know in the original story Aladdin was Chinese! The Princess is the daughter of a Chinese Emperor and the city that the sorceror is from is in Africa, not Arabia, it was added to 1001 nights by a French Men. Both the stories and the Story behind the stories are very international.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, amazingly Western culture is not the first one to Exoticize the foreign, Aladdin appears to have come from either an Arabic of Persian source and used China as &quot;weird foreign place we've heard of&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}